WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:04.520
Speaker 1: There's some interesting news,
which is it's good news, but it's also not

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:05.590
nearly enough.

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:10.139
New York is going to be raising the age to
buy an assault rifle from 18 to 21.

00:00:10.139 --> 00:00:14.200
And New York is going to be banning body armor.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.230
Widely reported, including by Bloomberg.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:20.910
Governor Kathy Hochul and legislative leaders
pledged to raise the legal age to purchase

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:26.840
an Air 15 assault rifle in New York to 21
from 18 and pass a package of measures to

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:32.360
tighten gun laws before the end of the state's
legislative session this week, citing the

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:34.540
mass shootings in Buffalo, New York and Nevada.

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:40.530
Texas local officials say they want to close
loopholes and address the gaps in laws exposed

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:42.470
by the back to back massacres.

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:47.160
The bills would prohibit the purchase of body
armor for civilians, require a license to

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:53.010
purchase a semiautomatic rifle, make threatening
mass harm a crime, and strengthen the state's

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:54.480
red flag laws.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:58.630
The measures would also require new pistols
to have micro stamping technology, which uses

00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:04.879
lasers to implant marked imprint markings
to make it easier to trace guns to registered

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:06.100
owners.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:14.750
Illinois, Washington, Hawaii and Florida have
already raised the age from 18 to 21 for assault

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:15.750
rifles.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:17.240
So this is great, right?

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:21.030
But neighboring Pennsylvania, you still only
have to be 18.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.369
To buy an assault rifle in neighboring New
Jersey.

00:01:23.369 --> 00:01:26.690
You still have to be only 18 to buy an assault
rifle.

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:32.030
And in New Jersey, adults can buy and use
bulletproof vests and body armor unless you

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:34.020
have a felony conviction.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:39.330
And in Pennsylvania, there are no extra body
armor regulations besides federal laws.

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:42.510
So in Pennsylvania, adults can still buy and
use bulletproof vests.

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:43.540
And you could say, well.

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:46.689
But David, it would be against the law to
cross state lines.

00:01:46.689 --> 00:01:47.689
Right.

00:01:47.689 --> 00:01:50.250
Yeah, but it's still extraordinarily easy
to do.

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:56.820
And so you get the idea we need some kind
of broader probably federal legislation on

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:58.360
a lot of this stuff.

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:04.329
Now, one of the things we have to remember
is if the crime is going to be where there's

00:02:04.329 --> 00:02:12.420
more population and we've got a piece planned
on this issue of the gun violence is in so-called

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:13.700
Democrat cities.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:18.860
You all know, as I've explained before, cities
in general lean, Democratic and high crime

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:23.180
cities and low crime cities are basically
run by Democrats.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:27.190
Democrats just live in cities and crime is
more prevalent where there is more population

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:28.190
density.

00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:32.870
So we might understand, well, the population
centers are where you're going to see more

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:33.870
crime.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:38.180
But if it's that easy for people to go to
Jersey and Pennsylvania for the weapons or

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:44.430
to go from Chicago into Indiana, this type
of thing might actually backfire statistically

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:48.920
in what shows up good for New York City, good
for the state of New York.

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:51.459
But we really need a national effort here.

00:02:51.459 --> 00:02:53.819
Now, in terms of 18 versus 21.

00:02:53.819 --> 00:03:00.020
I would actually go to 25 on semiautomatic
assault weapons now, you might say.

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:01.670
But, David, why not ban them altogether?

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:02.670
Sure.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:05.629
I'm trying to be realistic to some degree.

00:03:05.629 --> 00:03:12.300
And when you look at the ages of many of these
mass shooters, you have a situation where

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:20.080
you've overwhelmingly got shooters under 25
using a semiautomatic assault rifles.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:27.620
So you could deal with a ton of the mass shootings,
specifically by targeting those firearms and

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:28.620
those individuals.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:30.060
Now, of course, we should be doing much more.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:37.200
And as I've said before, what you do to deal
with gun suicides versus individual gun homicides

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:42.400
versus mass shootings, three different problems,
three different sets of solutions.

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.670
We talked about this Tuesday on the bonus
show with Pat.

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:49.080
But this is at least one thing that can be
done.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:55.440
And, you know, unfortunately, in my interview
in the last segment, Congressman Jamie Raskin

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:59.770
was not super optimistic that this time it's
going to go differently in terms of getting

00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:02.170
Republicans on board to actually do something.

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:06.849
But even though it's not enough, even though
it doesn't go far enough, even though it's

00:04:06.849 --> 00:04:12.190
not happening in enough places to make a difference,
yet New York is at least doing something.

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:17.339
Listen, Canada is doing more as a result of
mass shootings in the United States than the

00:04:17.339 --> 00:04:18.959
United States is doing.

00:04:18.959 --> 00:05:35.729
And we'll talk about that on the bonus show.

